#: includes/Admin/DocumentationPage.php:46
#: includes/Admin/DocumentationPage.php:47
msgid "Delivery Table"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/DocumentationPage.php:92
msgid "How to use it"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/views/documentation.php:26
msgid "Attribute"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/views/documentation.php:27
msgid "What it does"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/views/documentation.php:28
msgid "Example"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/views/documentation.php:49
msgid "This plugin reads your Flexible Shipping zones and cost rules and turns them into a delivery price table. There is nothing to configure here: change a rule in Flexible Shipping and the table follows."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/views/documentation.php:56
msgid "How to place the table"
msgstr ""

#. translators: 1: shortcode, 2: block name.
#: includes/Admin/views/documentation.php:62
#, php-format
msgid "Use the shortcode %1$s, or add the \"Delivery Table\" block (%2$s) in the editor. Both render the same table through the same code."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/views/documentation.php:71
msgid "Columns are order value ranges, built from every price change and every free shipping threshold across the methods in the table. Rows are your shipping methods."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/views/documentation.php:81
msgid "Shipping zone name or id. Leave empty to render a table for every zone."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/views/documentation.php:85
msgid "Zone headings: auto (only when several zones are shown), show, or hide."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/views/documentation.php:89
msgid "How to show tax: auto (follow the WooCommerce cart setting), incl (always add shipping VAT), excl (always net)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/views/documentation.php:93
msgid "Split the output into a prepaid table and a cash-on-delivery table by matching this text in the method title. Empty means one table."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/views/documentation.php:97
msgid "Include shipping methods that are switched off. Default: no."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/views/documentation.php:101
msgid "Also render the implicit \"Locations not covered by your other zones\" zone."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/views/documentation.php:107
msgid "How to read the table"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/views/documentation.php:112
#: src/shipping-table/edit.js:55
msgid "Zone headings"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/views/documentation.php:115
msgid "Headings show the zone regions translated into the storefront language, so an English shop reads \"Germany\" where a German one reads \"Deutschland\". That is the region, not the zone name you typed in wp-admin. Postcodes limit a zone rather than name it, so they are left out."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/views/documentation.php:123
msgid "Zones grouped by region"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/views/documentation.php:126
msgid "Several zones covering the same place are shown together under one heading, in the order you arranged them, however far apart they sit in wp-admin. A zone covering several countries at once keeps its own combined heading. Each region carries an anchor built from its country codes, such as #dtfs-region-de or #dtfs-region-de-fr, so you can link straight to one table."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/views/documentation.php:134
msgid "Methods WooCommerce provides itself"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/views/documentation.php:137
msgid "Flat rate, local pickup and free shipping are priced from their own settings, and Flexible Shipping's rules take over whenever they are switched on for one of those methods. A flat rate whose cost is a formula rather than a fixed amount depends on the basket, not the order value, so it shows a dash."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/views/documentation.php:145
msgid "A dash instead of a price"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/views/documentation.php:148
msgid "No cost rule in that method covers that order value, for example when the method is priced by weight rather than by order value. The table says so instead of guessing."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/views/documentation.php:156
msgid "An asterisk after a price"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/views/documentation.php:159
msgid "The amount is right for that order value, but the same Flexible Shipping rule also depends on something the table cannot show - weight, item count, or a free shipping coupon. Hover the asterisk for the detail."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/views/documentation.php:167
#: src/shipping-table/edit.js:75
msgid "Tax"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/views/documentation.php:170
msgid "By default the table follows the WooCommerce setting \"Display prices during cart and checkout\", so a gross-priced shop gets gross prices and a net-priced shop gets net ones. Override it per table with the tax attribute."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/views/documentation.php:180
msgid "For developers"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/views/documentation.php:182
msgid "Template function"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/views/documentation.php:197
msgid "Overriding the markup"
msgstr ""

#. translators: 1: plugin folder name, 2: theme folder name.
#: includes/Admin/views/documentation.php:203
#, php-format
msgid "Copy a file from the plugin's %1$s folder into %2$s in your theme and edit it there. Child theme wins over parent theme, exactly like WooCommerce templates."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/views/documentation.php:210
msgid "Hooks"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/views/documentation.php:216
msgid "Action. Fires once every service is registered; receives the service container."
msgstr ""

